\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.3}{\ignorespaces \small  Statistical Ensembles (NVT, NPT, and Grand Canonical). The microcanonical ensemble is not practically interesting. If you want to talk to experimentalists, they will ask you to simulate a NPT ensemble instead. This is fairly difficult. Keeping fixed temperature (NVT) is already tricky, but also putting the pressure constant is even more. The most difficult ensemble to simulate is the grand canonical. Why whould you actually wish to simulate that? For example, to underatand what water molecules do going in and out from an internal cavity of a protein.}}{77}{figure.caption.48}\protected@file@percent }
